Bash Notes
Man Pages
-------------

man = manual

man pages open in less

man pages typically have sections
 - man 1 cp
 - (Section 1 of copy command)

help is the man equivalent built into Bash

ZSH does not have help built in
ZSH has run-help built in

When finding files, which / where / type -a, can be useful

which command only finds external while type -a will find everything about it

type command tells you what the command is
type -a will tell you every type from top to bottom

Some commands have more options in the built in version rather than the one on your system.
That's when you would need to use help rather than man to view the built in manual.

